                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "449c3880-3d4b-48c9-9fbb-633ed31236b1",
                        "entry_id": "d1dadd77-7aa3-3cef-9d17-810bcf7a1c51",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more parching"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9c9fa041-968d-4d84-9f15-191d909a665d",
                        "entry_id": "d1dadd77-7aa3-3cef-9d17-810bcf7a1c51",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most parching"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "730f4550-3661-3f1f-adf1-c9b109b93f7c",
                        "entry_id": "d1dadd77-7aa3-3cef-9d17-810bcf7a1c51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Causing something or someone to parch; extremely drying."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "16c73adf-bc83-4205-a1f5-42a3ba6b8984",
                                "sense_id": "730f4550-3661-3f1f-adf1-c9b109b93f7c",
                                "text": "Who can unpitying see the flowery race, / Shed by the morn, their new-flush'd bloom resign, / Before the parching beam?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4271f5ad-e186-4457-83b7-502cbdfca572",
                                "sense_id": "730f4550-3661-3f1f-adf1-c9b109b93f7c",
                                "text": "The desert storm was riding in its strength; the travellers lay beneath the mastery of the fell simoom.[…]Drifts of yellow vapour, fiery, parching, stinging, filled the air."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "90006356-b475-4c13-96f0-dda85b658839",
                                "sense_id": "730f4550-3661-3f1f-adf1-c9b109b93f7c",
                                "text": "The series of these great events began in the year 1333, fifteen years before the plague broke out in Europe: they first appeared in China. Here a parching drought, accompanied by famine, commenced in the tract of country watered by the rivers Kiang and Hoai."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "49316b54-0cb8-474c-878f-92eaeabe7ece",
                                "sense_id": "730f4550-3661-3f1f-adf1-c9b109b93f7c",
                                "text": "I began also to feel very hungry, as not having eaten for twenty-four hours; and worse than that, there was a parching thirst and dryness in my throat, and nothing with which to quench it."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "72ef45a9-f989-3f41-af77-d68b328da671",
                        "entry_id": "d1dadd77-7aa3-3cef-9d17-810bcf7a1c51",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Very thirsty; parched."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bbde43c-4295-4c55-ac10-42d46a6c6be2",
                                "sense_id": "72ef45a9-f989-3f41-af77-d68b328da671",
                                "text": "Proceed to nearest canteen and there annex liquor stores. March! Tramp, tramp, tramp the boys are […] parching."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6e2bc2b4-2882-3b77-aa74-04565fda44ca",
                "word": "parching",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "3f3ffa32-bdd9-4326-a8d1-520a02fb6b04",
                        "entry_id": "6e2bc2b4-2882-3b77-aa74-04565fda44ca",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "parchings"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "54b72725-6a26-37bf-9cc5-5e440aa7e8e2",
                        "entry_id": "6e2bc2b4-2882-3b77-aa74-04565fda44ca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The process of parching or roasting something, such as corn."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbe77946-9f82-49ed-8103-528444c2bc5d",
                                "sense_id": "54b72725-6a26-37bf-9cc5-5e440aa7e8e2",
                                "text": "I have already told how we parched sunflower seed; and that I used two or three double-handfuls of seed to a parching. I used two parchings of sunflower seed for one mess of four-vegetables-mixed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "df042cdd-72bd-39e4-a43a-0522deccbf42",
                        "entry_id": "6e2bc2b4-2882-3b77-aa74-04565fda44ca",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The condition of being parched; absolute dryness."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c048792-6b31-4ffc-bc0f-4754a8a3b5a4",
                                "sense_id": "df042cdd-72bd-39e4-a43a-0522deccbf42",
                                "text": "Squalid youths with ghastly grin,\nIn hollow bitter roots shall bring,\nUrine of the unsav'ry goat,\nTo quell the parchings of thy throat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
